# ── Driver output directories (2026-07-03 figure-hygiene policy, D4) ──────────
# Figures are DERIVED ARTIFACTS. The driver + its committed input data are the
# artifact of record; the rendered binary is regenerable and NOT tracked by
# default. Only figures CITED from a .tex/.md (via \includegraphics / markdown
# image / an explicit path reference) are committed — those live in the
# volumes' `figures/` dirs, which are NOT matched below.
#
# These are the deterministic driver scratch dirs (regenerate by re-running the
# driver named in the sibling result-doc / test). Anything here is safe to lose.
# Policy note: manuscript/ave-kb/common/engine-capability-map.md §8.
src/tests/outputs/
src/scripts/**/_output/
**/simulations/outputs/
# (manuscript/**/figures/ is deliberately NOT ignored — those are the tracked,
#  cited render targets. A cited figure that a driver writes into a `figures/`
#  dir stays tracked; only the scratch `_output`/`outputs` dirs are ignored.)
#
# EXCEPTIONS — 16 CITED figures still live inside these scratch dirs. The bulk
# of this block was RETIRED 2026-08-20 by the Phase-2 figure/data migration
# (29 renders + 49 data artifacts moved to their tracked homes per the ratified
# policy, `_orchestration/2026-07_repo-conventions.md` §(a) + :12; destinations
# at `_orchestration/docket-entries/2026-08-20-phase2-destination-map.md`).
# What REMAINS is exactly two sets, and both are deliberate:
#   9 · src/scripts — the HELD flag set, not yet ruled:
#       · the 3 `vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_*` .pdf/.png PAIRS — one
#         `style.save()` call emits both formats to one stub, so the pair is one
#         unit and the pdf/png allowlist contradiction is its own open question;
#       · 3 renders (`a1_spatial_cavity_mode_fft.png`,
#         `two_natured_electron_native_engine.png`,
#         `optical_caustic_resolution.png`) whose BYTE-IDENTICAL twin is already
#         tracked in the destination's own \graphicspath — moving them would put
#         two same-named blobs on one graphics path, and retiring the twin is a
#         DELETION on the D15c orphan-data axis, which this lane was not ruled
#         to touch.
#   7 · src/tests/outputs — never in the migration's scope.
# The count above is DERIVED from the lines below (not hand-maintained), so it
# cannot drift the way the old "38" did — that number was stale against a
# HEAD-true 32 for over a month. Re-derive on any change.
!src/scripts/vol_4_engineering/outputs/optical_caustic_resolution.png
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/a1_spatial_cavity_mode_fft.png
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/two_natured_electron_native_engine.png
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_signal_vs_field.pdf
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_signal_vs_field.png
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_time_to_5sigma.pdf
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_time_to_5sigma.png
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_window_E_vs_g.pdf
!src/scripts/vol_9_device/_output/vacuum_birefringence_facility_sweep_window_E_vs_g.png
!src/tests/outputs/beryllium_9_density_equator.png
!src/tests/outputs/beryllium_9_density_z_pos.png
!src/tests/outputs/boron_11_density_equator.png
!src/tests/outputs/ee_network_analysis.png
